Sval: browser_490040.js opens each window without the workspace the last one left

A window takes a workspace no other window shows and opens that workspace's
tabs (spec §10.7), and closing a window keeps its workspace once a page was
browsed in it (decision 0101). The test's first window browses
example.com, so each later window it opens shows that workspace, and once
Sval restores its tab the window holds a page and is saved as a recently
closed window, which the test counts as a window that must not be. Whether
the tab lands before the test closes the window is a race. The harness
removes such workspaces between files (SvalTestLeftovers.sys.mjs); a file
has no hook between its own windows, so the test calls it before each one.

